{
  "_doc": [
    "Semantic tile palette for Gray Stone. Maps are generated from semantic symbols",
    "and resolved to numeric MZ tile IDs through this file, so a wrong visual slot is",
    "corrected HERE and the maps are regenerated -- never by hand-editing MapXXX.json.",
    "",
    "'verify' records how much confidence the binding carries:",
    "  CALCULATED  - follows from the engine's own tile-ID arithmetic. Certain.",
    "  SPEC        - the workbook (68_Prologue_Tile_Palette) names this exact kind.",
    "  SHEET_READ  - read off the actual tileset sheet by eye. Large, unambiguous",
    "                colour fields (A3 roof/wall families) are reliable; small B-sheet",
    "                objects may still be off by a cell.",
    "  ASSUMED     - a plausible slot that has NOT been checked against the art.",
    "  CONFIRMED   - verified against tools/out/tiles-<sheet>.html.",
    "",
    "Verify with:  node tools/pick_tiles.js   then open tools/out/tiles-<sheet>.html",
    "",
    "Autotile IDs:  2048 + kind*48 + shape   (shape is solved by the map builder)",
    "'kind' is the ENGINE-GLOBAL kind, not the per-sheet index the workbook uses:",
    "  A1 0-15 | A2 16-47 | A3 48-79 | A4 80-127, eight kinds per palette row.",
    "  A2 local (col,row) -> 16+row*8+col;  A3 -> 48+row*8+col;  A4 -> 80+row*8+col.",
    "Normal tiles:  B=0 C=256 D=512 E=768, id = base + row*16 + col  (A5: 1536+row*8+col)",
    "",
    "Sheet C is avoided on purpose: in this asset set the C sheets are modern city",
    "content (cars, neon, vending machines) and Gray Stone is 1896.",
    "Sheet B col 0 row 0 is unusable: its tile id is 0, which the engine treats as an empty cell."
  ],
